    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners have already been created today (by `registrationDate`).\n\nChanges, following the existing city-capacity rule as the template:\n\n1. **`rest/validation/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `CityCapacityExceededException`.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 `createOwner(...)` now calls `rejectWhenDailyLimitReached(owner)` first. It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's day (which the controller defaults to `LocalDate.now()`), and throws when the count is `>= 100` (constant `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT`). The count is evaluated pre-persist, consistent with the sibling city/namesake rules.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) as a `ProblemDetail`, matching the format of the other handlers.\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, then expect the 101st to be 429) passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: no git repo is present here, so nothing was committed.",
